  <h1>Carpool vs flying: San Francisco to Los Angeles and LA to Las Vegas</h1>
  <div class="meta">Updated September 2026 · Prices are typical ranges; live seat prices are on each route page</div>

  <p class="lede"><strong>Short answer:</strong> flying is 2 to 3 hours faster door to door on San Francisco to Los Angeles and costs 2 to 4 times as much once bags and the airport legs are counted. A Seat Sherpa carpool seat is capped at $55 plus a 5% fee, leaves from a pickup point you agree in chat, and takes 6 to 7.5 hours. Flying wins on time; the carpool wins on money, luggage and everything around the flight.</p>

  <h2>The honest door-to-door numbers</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th>SF to LA</th><th>Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)</th><th>Seat Sherpa seat</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Fare</td><td data-l="Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)">$60 to $200 advance; $150 to $300+ same week</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">$30 to $55 + 5% fee, any time</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bags</td><td data-l="Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)">$35 to $80 for a checked bag on basic fares</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">Included by arrangement with the driver</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Getting to and from airports</td><td data-l="Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)">$30 to $90 in transit or rideshare, both ends</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">Pickup near you; drop-off arranged in chat</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Time</td><td class="win" data-l="Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)">4 to 5 h door to door: 90-minute flight plus security and transfers</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">6 to 7.5 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Typical all-in</td><td data-l="Flying (SFO/OAK to LAX/BUR)">$150 to $350</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">$35 to $60</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>LA to Las Vegas is closer: a 1-hour flight for $40 to $150 plus bags, about 3.5 to 4.5 hours door to door, against 4.5 to 5.5 hours and $25 to $55 plus fee in a carpool.</p>

  <h2>When to fly anyway</h2>
  <p>When the hours matter more than the money, when you are travelling light on a fare booked weeks out, or when a connection at the other end depends on a fixed arrival time. Weather rarely affects either option on these routes; I-5 traffic and airport security lines are the wildcards.</p>

  <div class="callout" style="text-align:center">
